{"They were to call for her at her house in the Taurida Gardens at ten o’clock, but it was already \003five minutes to ten\004, and the girls were not yet dressed.\nNatásha was going to her first grand ball. She had got up at eight that morning and had been in a fever of excitement and activity all day.","War and Peace","Leo Tolstoy",true},
